			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-27T20:18:39Z",
			"File": [
				"⡇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				3
			],
			"Message": "fix(Project): Add DI decorator metadata to ReplaceSearchService and sync submodules\n\nSubmodule synchronization across Common, Output, and Cocoon:\n\n1. Output (46eceea1): Add DI decorator metadata to ReplaceSearchService transform - The ReplaceSearchService transform was missing TypeScript-compiled decorator helpers (__decorate, __param) that VS Code's DI container requires to resolve constructor parameters by their @IService decorator types. Without these, IInstantiationService bound parameters positionally with no type knowledge, causing all dependencies to arrive as undefined and crashing on this.uriIdentityService.extUri. This commit adds the __decorate/__param runtime helpers mirrored from VS Code's compiled output, enabling proper service resolution for IModelService, IEditorService, ITelemetryService, ILogService, IExtensionService, IFileService, IInstantiationService, and IUriIdentityService. The search panel now properly delegates to Mountain's search:findFiles/search:findInFiles handlers via Tauri IPC.\n\n2. Common (056b8d26): Sync with Current branch, includes dependabot update to @cloudflare/workers-types from 4.20260424.1 to 4.20260426.1\n\n3. Cocoon (f78bc413): Forward sync to latest Current\n\nImpact: Search panel now functions correctly with .gitignore-aware file search via Mountain handlers.",
			"SHA": "4f9670ef93d4a556b367a6799133adb6b4360976"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-27T19:54:45Z",
			"File": [
				"⡿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				5
			],
			"Message": "feat(Project): Add debug session tracking, custom editor events, and search service transform\n\nSubmodule synchronization bringing three major features:\n\n1. Debug Session Tracking (Mountain + Common + Sky):\n- Mountain implements DebugSessionEntry and DebugSessions map for lifecycle management\n- StartDebugging spawns DAP adapters with stdin/stdout/stderr pipes and parses DAP frames\n- Messages emitted on `sky://debug/dap-message` and forwarded to DOM events\n- StopDebugging sends DAP disconnect and unregisters the session\n- Common adds DebugDapMessage IPC event to support this flow\n\n2. Custom Editor Save Events (Mountain + Common + Sky):\n- Common adds CustomEditorSaved IPC event for UI notifications\n- Mountain implements OnSaveCustomDocument to reverse-RPC to Cocoon extension sidecar\n- Sky adds handler for `sky://customEditor/saved` dispatching cel:customEditor:saved\n\n3. Search Service Replacement (Output):\n- Add ReplaceSearchService transform replacing web-worker RemoteSearchService\n- Delegates to Mountain's `search:findFiles` / `search:findInFiles` handlers\n- Makes search .gitignore-aware via Rust's ignore::WalkBuilder\n- Fixes search panel showing 0 matches and node_modules appearing in results\n\n4. Bug Fixes (Mountain):\n- Fix char-aware UTF-8 truncation in WindServiceHandlers and OutputChannelAppend\n- Avoids panics when slicing multi-byte codepoints (e.g., `•` in SCM progress)\n\nImpact: Debugging now works with real DAP adapters, custom editor save callbacks notify observers, and file search respects .gitignore rules.",
			"SHA": "15e5ce0a3c99ee27478c2ac3496e8ce21d53cd11"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-27T15:55:13Z",
			"File": [
				"⡟⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				4
			],
			"Message": "fix(Project): Align SCM provider handles between Mountain and Cocoon\n\nSubmodule synchronization addressing two critical issues:\n\n1. SCM Provider Handle Alignment (Common + Mountain + Cocoon):\n   - Common adds optional Handle field to SourceControlCreateDTO enabling Cocoon to supply its sequential allocator handle\n   - Mountain now honors caller-supplied Handle in CreateSourceControl rather than allocating via DJB hash\n   - Previously, group updates from Cocoon used sequential handles while Mountain keyed marker maps with DJB hash, causing \"Received group update for unknown provider handle\" warnings and empty SCM viewlet\n\n2. Recently-Opened Workspace Fallback (Mountain):\n   - Fixes boot seeding to probe RecentlyOpened.json (same source as webview's BuildInitialUrl) between env/CLI and CWD walk-up\n   - Resolves webview title showing \"Mountain\" while Cocoon payload shipped \"Land\"\n   - Fixes vscode.git scanning wrong root and SCM panel showing zeros despite untracked changes\n\n3. Dependency Updates:\n   - Mountain, Worker: Bump pozil/auto-assign-issue from 2.2.x to 3.0.0\n\nRefs: 3cfc021e (DTO serialization), 4c472e3 (event payload fixes)",
			"SHA": "072ef07cf9596928526c3330aedccd96136239b6"
		}
	],
